## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **Initial TD-43 v1 scope (EpisodeAssetDrawer only)** — failed because: Director's actual workflow opens VID-shot in the AssetPreview drawer (visible as «PREVIEW 2/22» header), NOT EpisodeAssetDrawer. Picker rendered but invisible on the surface Director used. Fixed in TD-43.B by mirroring to AssetPreview.tsx + threading `onPickAsset` through PreviewDrawer.
- **Initial SH01 video v02 (legacy direct VGEN path)** — failed because: ANIMATOR_CHAIN_ENABLED wasn't set when animatic was first approved. Approve-route fired `exec-vgen/start` directly (legacy buildShotPromptV2 template) → produced bedroom-default-layout video with weak prompt. Loss of $1.21 acceptable as baseline for legacy vs plan-driven comparison.
- **Polина initial Animator trigger** — failed because: she fired episode-level `exec-vanim/plan` without `shotId` → EXEC-VANIM correctly rejected with «requires shotId in event payload». Fix was on Polина's side: per-shot triggerAgent calls (she self-corrected after Director's «одобряю» on q1).
- **TD-43.C initial hover popover** — failed because: 8px gap between cell wrapper and popover (`-top-2 -translate-y-full`) → cursor crossing the gap fired mouseLeave on wrapper → popover hid. Fix: change to `top-0 -translate-y-full` so popover bottom edge sits exactly at cell top — no gap (commit `5aa8e5c`).
- **SH01 plan v02 quality_tier extraction** — failed because: Animator wrote `provider.id="seedance-standard"` AND `quality_tier="standard"` in Plan body, but runner.ts q7a Step 6 extracted them INDEPENDENTLY. provider was resolved from event-arg / DB-config (Seedance fast default), `body.quality_tier` was ignored because the plan-driven path didn't reach actual override before VGEN call. Result: SH01 video came out `bytedance/seedance-2.0/fast/image-to-video` despite Plan saying standard. Closed by TD-44 (`resolveVanimProviderId()` makes provider.id authoritative for both providerImpl AND qualityTier).

